    "AI Notes": {
      "value": "Type foundry founded 2009 by Anthony Sheret and Edd Harrington, who also run The Entente, their design studio launched a few months earlier; offices in London and Los Angeles, team of about eight (LinkedIn lists 2 to 10). Known for Apercu (2010, widely adopted, used by MoMA), Value Sans/Serif, Fortescue, and custom type commissions for brands including Burger King, Canva, Cadillac and Instagram (Instagram Sans). Acquired by Monotype in December 2023; as of March 2025 the standalone colophon-foundry.org store closed and the library folded into Monotype Fonts and MyFonts, though co-founder quotes suggest the team continues custom work under the Colophon name within Monotype, so kept as Studio rather than Unknown. No direct public email found, site now routes contact through Monotype sales; flagged as an open question.",
